KG42.register("clusters-c5933221a632e09fbb88ebce",{"id":"15-multiagent_reverse_auction::v142-d-K002","paper":"15-multiagent_reverse_auction","label":"Branch candidates for qualified supplier selection, auction termination, and clearing price","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K002","label":"Branch candidates for qualified supplier selection, auction termination, and clearing price","market_meaning":"The aggregator determines qualified suppliers and forms a clearing price in repeated bidding. Both the single-remaining-supplier path in the general description and the simultaneous two-supplier path in the example are retained; the existing chains are not yet sufficient to give unified termination and pricing rules.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["coordination","matching","pricing"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"The general description, pseudocode, and hour-17 example of the same mechanism have different termination and pricing statements. Shared R006 only provides the price-reduction request interface under excess supply and cannot be used to prove a unique termination condition; the example conditions cannot be generalized unconditionally.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The supplier eligibility result is a direct condition of the pricing branch, and the two should be checked together. This cluster takes eligibility and the clearing-price result as its boundary, retains the interface with bid interaction, and does not create a new scientific edge merely from procedural order.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Carries the multi-supplier permission and the single-remaining-supplier termination description; how their applicability connects still needs to be clarified."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R010","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Carries the pricing branch of the general clearing-price description and the two-supplier example, retaining all uncertain references."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Only borrows the condition under which excess supply triggers a price-reduction request, providing an entry point for the discussion of eligibility and termination; its primary ownership remains with the bid-interaction cluster."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E17"],"rationale":"The same passage connects re-bidding at a reduced price under excess supply with the statement that only one qualified bidder remains; the mapping records this process association and does not determine that it has resolved all stopping cases."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g02-e012"],"rationale":"The general pricing description explicitly uses the case in which a single qualified bidder remains, so there is a conditional interface between the eligibility result and price determination; the other bidder to which the price refers remains unspecified."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-e021"],"rationale":"When a single seller cannot meet demand, multiple qualified sellers are permitted, which is compatible with the scope in the example where two suppliers jointly meet demand. Here only the applicable cases are compared; it is not presumed that a complete rule for transferring from the single-supplier branch to the two-supplier branch has been given."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::V::matching.counterparties","v141-c-R010::V::matching.counterparties"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g02-e012","v141-b-g02-e021"],"rationale":"The two references belong to the same supplier-matching function node; the general termination description and the qualified set in the example cannot be directly equated, so their respective intra-chain contexts are retained."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G01","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The general description terminates when only one qualified bidder remains, whereas the example ends when two suppliers are simultaneously qualified and the submitted quantity meets demand. The pseudocode additionally has demand => total bid submitted supply; the meaning of its operator and the loop direction cannot be arbitrarily determined from the order of the narrative.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g02-e003","v141-b-g02-e012","v141-b-g02-e021"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the original pseudocode and context to clarify the branch conditions and priorities for a single supplier, multiple suppliers, and supply-demand satisfaction; if this cannot be clarified, continue to retain the conflict and do not fabricate a unified stopping predicate."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G02","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The specific bidder, round, and ordering references of last second qualified bidder and last bid are undefined; they cannot be replaced with the standard second-price formula merely on the basis of the Vickrey name, nor can the two price sources be taken to be the same.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e012","v141-b-g02-e021"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Determine the ordered bid record and the source definitions of each price reference; if there is no clear basis, retain the two scoped procedural descriptions and do not select a unified price representative."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G03","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The clearing price, the relevant bid prices, the total submitted power, and demand all lack typed quantity objects and mathematical bindings in this chain; the general meaning of meets demand is not specified as equality or sufficiency. Existing function nodes cannot replace these quantities.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R010::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e012","v141-b-g02-e021"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"According to the existing C2 revision request, upstream should verify the quantity roles, units, indices, and usable expressions; example data can only be retained as examples, and where definitions are lacking, not_formalized is maintained."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G04","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The example text uses hour 17 and kW, whereas the title of the figure transcription is hour 16 and the procurement log uses W. Whether the difference is a time-index numbering or simulation-scaling difference cannot yet be determined.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e019","v141-b-g02-e020","v141-b-g02-e021"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the hour numbering and unit conventions in the original figure, the main text, and Table II; before they are clarified, do not merge the log quantities and the example quantities in the main text into the same parameter."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G05","category":"unverified_source","description":"The B entries on which eligibility, stopping, and pricing are based are all unverified; this cluster presents checkable candidate associations and does not mean that the transcription or the Vickrey interpretation has passed review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g02-e012","v141-b-g02-e019","v141-b-g02-e020","v141-b-g02-e021"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check each chain, source location, example scope, and assembly mapping; maintain the current unreviewed status, and this candidate cannot replace independent source verification."}]},"rule_refs":["15-multiagent_reverse_auction::v141-c-R008","15-multiagent_reverse_auction::v141-c-R010","15-multiagent_reverse_auction::v141-c-R006"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-334f35169e6933ed","COMP-8ae9e2dee736e7c9","COMP-97d6b21fedc8f7d3","COMP-b646a091517c6af0","COMP-bb3ab287e4b08dc8"]});
